				<td id="mainbody">
				
				<table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" class="listtable">
					<tr valign="top">
						<td width="25%" nowrap style="padding-top: 11px;"><p class="subhead2">May 15, 2001</p></td>
						<td width="75%"><p class="bodycopysans"><span class="subhead1">Shaye R. Mandle</span></p>
						<p class="bodycopysmall">Shaye R. Mandle is the president of the Illinois Coalition of Science and Technology. The Illinois Coalition, a nonprofit organization established in 1989, focuses its efforts on supporting scientific research and technology development throughout the state of Illinois. Shaye will offer his perspective on Illinois' role in the arenas of science and technology.</p></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td colspan="2" class="grayrulebottom"><img src="../images/common/spacer.gif" alt="" width="420" height="9" border="0"></td>
					</tr>
					<tr valign="top">
						<td nowrap style="padding-top: 11px;"><p class="subhead2">April 10, 2001</p></td>
						<td><p class="bodycopysans"><span class="subhead1">Andrew "Flip" Filipowski</span></p>
						<p class="bodycopysmall">Andrew "Flip" Filipowski is the chairman and chief executive officer of divine, inc., a Chicago-based enterprise Web solutions company. divine is focused on developing and marketing critical software infrastructure and technology solutions for enterprises worldwide, as well as the integration, training, and sales and marketing services to support those solutions. divine also holds interests in various companies that are principally involved in integrated solutions for e-commerce and vertical markets. Flip will offer his perspective on the volatility within the technology sector and address divine's position and strategy in the software and technology marketplace.</p></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td colspan="2" class="grayrulebottom"><img src="../images/common/spacer.gif" alt="" width="420" height="9" border="0"></td>
					</tr>
					<tr valign="top">
						<td nowrap style="padding-top: 11px;"><p class="subhead2">February 13, 2001</p></td>
						<td><p class="bodycopysans"><span class="subhead1">David Weinstein</span></p>
						<p class="bodycopysmall">David Weinstein, President and Chief Executive Officer of BlueMeteor, a Chicago-based e-business service provider, will be the featured speaker. Weinstein will offer his perspective on the current volatility of Chicago's technology-related start-ups and solution providers.</p></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td colspan="2" class="grayrulebottom"><img src="../images/common/spacer.gif" alt="" width="420" height="9" border="0"></td>
					</tr>
					<tr valign="top">
						<td nowrap style="padding-top: 11px;"><p class="subhead2">December 7, 2000</p></td>
						<td><p class="bodycopysmall">Meet five dynamic online community thought leaders during an evening of discussion, dining and debate. Learn what it takes to launch, nurture and leverage many-to-many discussions in every type of Internet environment - from publicly accessible vertical sites to Intranet knowledge networks to customer communities centered around products and services. Discover the benefits of hosting community spaces while avoiding common community pitfalls.</p></td>
					</tr>
				</table>
				
